 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Color Space:** The method must be applied in RGB color space. Implementations in YCoCg or YCrCb color spaces produced excessive flickering and were deemed infeasible [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Spot Light Variance:** Near the origin of spot lights, sub-froxel jittering causes sampled values to jump from zero to high intensity, creating high variance. This is mitigated by introducing a minimum distance threshold of $0.5$ meters for spot light intensity calculations; samples closer than this use the minimum distance [S1, unofficial]. This reduces fireflies but makes the spot light attenuation shape less visually distinct [S1, unofficial].
